{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "target" %}
{# render_mode guard MUST be within the first 5 lines (see 0330). #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{# Relationships - the wedding planner (2.5, Build B, M4p; the author,         #}
{# 2026-10-20)                                                                #}
{#                                                                            #}
{# Five priestesses plan weddings for a fee (Officiant.cpp, kPlannerNames).   #}
{# Hired, they help the couple settle the plan and compose the ceremony;      #}
{# the rings are chosen here, except for an elopement. Silent unless the      #}
{# player is engaged. get_wedding_planner is native.                          #}
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% if not is_player(actorUUID) %}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esl") or is_plugin_loaded("SNRom_Integration.esp") %}
{% set wp = get_wedding_planner(actorUUID) %}
{# ALWAYS SAID TO A PLANNER (2026-10-25): Danica Pure-Spring, asked about
   planning a wedding while the player was engaged to no one, did not know
   she planned weddings. What she plans waits for an engagement. #}
{% if wp and default(wp.planner, 0) == 1 %}

## Weddings

Beside your duties, you plan weddings: for a fee of {{ wp.fee }} gold you help a couple settle everything a wedding needs, and compose the ceremony with them.
{% if not existsIn(wp, "couples") or length(wp.couples) == 0 %}
{{ player.name }} is not engaged to anyone that you know of. A wedding begins with an engagement; once {{ player.name }} has asked someone and they have said yes, you would gladly plan it.
{% endif %}
{% for c in wp.couples %}
{% if default(c.hired, 0) == 1 %}

{# SETTLED SAYS SO (seen in play, wpm54): with the day and hour set and shown,
   Danica still answered "only the day and the hour" were left to decide. #}
{{ player.name }} has hired you to plan their wedding to {{ c.betrothed }}. As it stands - and whatever is set here is settled; ask about it again only if they want to change it: {% if c.plan.day != "" %}the day, {{ c.plan.day }}{% if default(c.plan.date, "") != "" %} ({{ c.plan.date }}){% endif %}{% else %}no day yet{% endif %}; {% if c.plan.place != "" %}the place, {{ c.plan.place }}{% if default(c.plan.spot, false) %}, the spot {{ player.name }} chose where they stood{% elif default(c.plan.near, "") != "" %} (by {{ c.plan.near }}){% endif %}{% else %}no place yet{% endif %}; {% if c.plan.officiant != "" %}{{ c.plan.officiant }} will marry them{% else %}no one is chosen to marry them yet: any priest or priestess in Skyrim they choose, yourself included, or the jarl of any hold, whoever holds it on the day; you send word, and they will come{% endif %}.{% if length(c.plan.guests) > 0 %} Invited: {% for g in c.plan.guests %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}
{# WHOSE GUESTS AND WHERE EVERYONE STANDS (wpm61; the author, 2026-10-28):
   each guest is one partner's, named by that partner, or both's; and the
   player marks where everyone stands by standing on each spot. #}
{% if length(default(c.plan.theirGuests, [])) > 0 %}{{ c.betrothed }}'s guests: {% for g in c.plan.theirGuests %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. {% endif %}{% if length(default(c.plan.yourGuests, [])) > 0 %}{{ player.name }}'s guests: {% for g in c.plan.yourGuests %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. {% endif %}{% if length(default(c.plan.bothGuests, [])) > 0 %}Guests of both: {% for g in c.plan.bothGuests %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. {% endif %}{% if length(default(c.plan.unsided, [])) > 0 %}Not yet known whose guests they are: {% for g in c.plan.unsided %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}
{% if c.plan.place != "" %}{% set marked = default(c.plan.marked, []) %}Where everyone will stand at {{ c.plan.place }}: {% if length(marked) == 0 %}nothing marked yet{% else %}marked for {% for m in marked %}{% if m == "officiant" %}{% if c.plan.officiant != "" %}{{ c.plan.officiant }}{% else %}the one who marries them{% endif %}{% elif m == "you" %}{{ player.name }}{% elif m == "betrothed" %}{{ c.betrothed }}{% elif m == "theirs" %}{{ c.betrothed }}'s guests{% else %}{{ player.name }}'s guests{% endif %}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.{# Marks, as a rule for this reply: at the end of the prompt since wpm88. #}{{ c.betrothed }} stands beside {{ player.name }} unless marked apart; each side's guests gather around their own mark, and anything unmarked gathers by the nearest that is.{% endif %}
The ceremony, as chosen so far: {% if c.plan.address == 1 %}an address to everyone gathered, {% endif %}{% if c.plan.reading == 1 %}a reading or blessing, {% endif %}the vows and each "do you take"{% if c.plan.rings == 1 %}, the rings exchanged{% endif %}, the pronouncement{% if c.plan.kiss == 1 %} and the kiss{% endif %}.
{# THE VOWS ARE THEIR OWN (wpm54): "beyond the vows" led Danica to offer
   "traditional vows or words of your own", a choice the ceremony does not
   have - and the parts it does have were never asked about. #}
The vows are always the couple's own: each speaks their own words to the other, and no one writes or recites vows for them, so there is nothing to choose about the vows. What the ceremony holds besides is four things, each in or out: the officiant's address to everyone gathered, a reading or blessing, the rings exchanged, the kiss.
The wedding rings: a man wears the wide plain band and a woman the slim set (the engagement ring joined to its band, for one who wears an engagement ring; otherwise the slim braided band), unless they choose otherwise - either may have either, whoever gave whom an engagement ring. Each is made in gold, silver or ebony, and they may choose the same. {{ c.betrothed }}'s: {{ c.plan.theirRing.style }}{% if default(c.plan.theirRing.usual, 0) == 1 %} (the usual one; there is no need to ask unless they want otherwise){% endif %}, {% if c.plan.theirRing.metal != "" %}{{ c.plan.theirRing.metal }}{% else %}metal not chosen{% endif %}. {{ player.name }}'s: {{ c.plan.yourRing.style }}{% if default(c.plan.yourRing.usual, 0) == 1 %} (the usual one; there is no need to ask unless they want otherwise){% endif %}, {% if c.plan.yourRing.metal != "" %}{{ c.plan.yourRing.metal }}{% else %}metal not chosen{% endif %}.
{% if length(c.plan.open) > 0 %}Still needed before the day can come: {% for o in c.plan.open %}{% if o == "day" %}the day{% elif o == "hour" %}the hour{% elif o == "place" %}where{% else %}who will marry them{% endif %}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}
{% if length(default(c.plan.unsettled, [])) > 0 %}Not yet talked through: {% for o in c.plan.unsettled %}{% if o == "near" %}what {{ c.plan.place }} is by (the temple, hall, inn or town nearest it), since no one can find their way there by that name alone{% elif o == "guests" %}who they will invite{% elif o == "sides" %}whose guests {% for g in c.plan.unsided %}{{ g }}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} are, {{ c.betrothed }}'s or {{ player.name }}'s{% elif o == "layout" %}where everyone will stand at {{ c.plan.place }}{% elif o == "ceremony" %}the ceremony's four parts (an address, a reading or blessing, the rings exchanged, the kiss){% elif o == "theirRing" %}the metal of {{ c.betrothed }}'s wedding ring{% elif o == "yourRing" %}the metal of {{ player.name }}'s wedding ring{% else %}what {{ c.betrothed }} will wear, theirs to choose and keep for the day{% endif %}{% if not loop.is_last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.{% endif %}
{# WHAT IT IS BY (seen in play, wpm59): "Under the Gildergreen" was no place
   anyone could be sent to, and no one came. "near" is unsettled once
   Relationships has looked for the place and found it nowhere. #}
{# The next question to ask: at the end of the prompt since wpm88 (user_final_instructions/8100_relationships_actions). #}
 Help as one who knows weddings: places that might suit them, who might come, what the ceremony could hold. What they choose is theirs, and anything settled can still be changed until the day: guests added or taken off, the day moved, the rings chosen again.{# SAYING IS NOT DOING (seen in play, wpm59): asked to take Brenuin off
   the list, Danica said "I have struck his name" and chose no action, so he
   stayed on it. #}{# That a change is made only by the Wedding action is said at the end of the prompt since wpm87 (user_final_instructions/8100_relationships_actions). #} What is written here is how the plan truly stands. You gave {{ player.name }} your book, which sets out every choice; point them to it when it helps. There is no shame in moving a wedding, so long as they tell you.
{% else %}

{{ player.name }} is engaged to {{ c.betrothed }}{% if c.plan.planner != "" %}, and {{ c.plan.planner }} is planning their wedding{% endif %}. If they ask, you could plan it for them, for your fee.
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
